Hi Phil,

Quick follow-up: I've only seen 'information' in IRT in reference to the item or test information functions. The matrix in @information clearly has a different interpretation because -- unless I am mistaken -- it is not a function of theta. I understand that this matrix is the inverse of the asymptotic covariance matrix of the ML item parameter estimates, but I'm having a difficult time figuring out how I can interpret the information matrix itself, i.e. without talking about what it means once we invert it. Is there any non-mathematical interpretation of this information matrix?

Thanks,
Jon

